<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (Using standard Frequentist and Bayesian with an uninformative prior distribution, yielded a one-sided p-value of more than 0.05 and a probability of greater than 70%. The results were inconclusive at both the overall experiment level and at more granular customer segments as sample size was too small to leverage either framework.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
